# Redaction map for `scripts/scrub.py --redact`.
#
# Copy to `.scrub-map.local` and fill in. That file is gitignored, because it
# necessarily contains the private strings it maps FROM.
#
# Format: <private string><TAB><placeholder>
# Longest matches are applied first, so a full hostname is replaced before any
# bare domain inside it.
#
# Use STABLE placeholders. The same host must become the same placeholder in
# every file, or migrated prose stops making sense — "connect to <HOST_1> then
# check <HOST_2>" is only readable if those are consistently the same machines.

# --- hosts and addresses -------------------------------------------------
# media.example-personal.xyz	<JELLYFIN_HOST>
# books.example-personal.xyz	<AUDIOBOOKSHELF_HOST>
# 10.13.37.20	<KODI_HOST>
# 10.13.37.21	<ANDROID_TV_HOST>
# 10.13.37.22	<DEVBOX_HOST>

# --- identity ------------------------------------------------------------
# /home/realname	/home/<user>
# realname	<user>
# realname@example.com	<email>

# --- devices -------------------------------------------------------------
# SOME_TV_MODEL_ID	<ANDROID_TV_MODEL>
# 10.13.37.21:44803	<ADB_SERIAL>

# --- credentials ---------------------------------------------------------
# Prefer rotating over redacting. A key that has been in a file an agent read
# should be treated as compromised regardless of what this map does to it.
# 0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef	<API_KEY>
# 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000	<USER_ID>

# --- shares --------------------------------------------------------------
# smb://somehost/somemedia	<SHARE>
